-# - LED SYNC: On connect, reads actual PulseAudio mute state and writes Note On/Off back to
-#   the LPD8 via amidi to sync pad LEDs to reality.  Each mute-state change also updates the LED.
-#   Action pads (3,5,8) briefly flash their LED on each trigger.
-#   NOTE: LED sync requires the LPD8 to be in NOTE TOGGLE mode in its hardware preset.
-#         In CC TOGGLE mode the hardware manages the LED itself; the startup sync still works
-#         for getting the initial state right after reboot.
+# - Startup reads the actual PulseAudio mute state to seed Hearth's internal toggle state.
+# - The attached classic LPD8 (USB VID:PID 09e8:0075) does not recognize incoming MIDI Note
+#   messages (per Akai's original MIDI implementation chart), so host-driven pad LED feedback
+#   is disabled. Physical pad illumination is controlled by the device itself. Do not report
+#   a MIDI write as visible LED initialization. LED feedback is opt-in for a controller known
+#   to support incoming Note On/Off messages via LED_FEEDBACK_SUPPORTED=1 in the config.
@@ -106,3 +106,6 @@
-# ---- LED feedback config ----
-# MIDI channel (0-indexed) used to send Note On/Off back to the LPD8 for LED control.
-# 9 = channel 10 (standard drum channel).  Override in roaring_mixer.conf as LED_MIDI_CHANNEL=9
+# ---- LED feedback capability/config ----
+# Default OFF for the classic LPD8 (USB VID:PID 09e8:0075), which cannot accept
+# incoming MIDI Note messages. Opt in only for a controller verified to support
+# host-driven pad LEDs by setting LED_FEEDBACK_SUPPORTED=1 in roaring_mixer.conf.
+LED_FEEDBACK_SUPPORTED=0
+# MIDI channel (0-indexed) used for supported devices; channel 10 by default.
@@ -110 +113 @@
